@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# The open grounds, cut tone on tone (desert, savanna, beach, plains)
+
+Art Director, 2026-10-27. Brief: the EP (relaying Orb's delegation), for the `signature` flash clip that fails in normal mode on main (3.5 of 5) since 22n's desert ground. Rendering's flip map: `docs/rendering/pending/2026-10-27k/README.md`. Tools: `art/concepts/biomes/ground.mjs`. Data: `data/art/biomes.json` (`palette.ground`, `scar`), regenerated through `gen.mjs` and `spec.mjs`.
+
+## What was measured
+
+On Rendering's still of main (`docs/rendering/img/lookgate/lookgate-sigdesert-faces-t91.png`) the desert's three ground faces draw as **the authored colour times 1.10 per channel, clipped at 255** (the front depth step; `RenderLook.DEPTH_STEP` is 1.10, 1.02 and 0.94 front to back):
+
+| Face | Authored | Drawn | Drawn luminance |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| lit | #ecd28c | #ffe79a | 0.807 |
+| mid | #d8b868 | #eeca73 | 0.617 |
+| shade | #a88a44 | #b9984b | 0.333 |
+
+The frame analyser counts a change of 0.1 or more where its darker side is under 0.8. The desert's faces sat 0.19 and 0.28 apart on both sides of that line, and as the split view pans, dunes turn over a face at a time. `ground.mjs` reproduces the table above to three places from the data, so the same figures can be read for any biome (`node art/concepts/biomes/ground.mjs`).
+
+## The rule
+
+**The three faces of an open ground stay within `PATTERN_BUDGET` (0.085 of relative luminance) of each other as drawn** (lit against shade, the widest pair, not only the neighbours), and are told apart by **hue**, not by value. Lit leans toward a paler yellow, shade toward a deeper orange (plains: lit toward yellow-green, shade toward blue-green). The faces stay 5 to 9 CIEDE2000 apart. Drawn values are at the front depth step; the other two steps scale every face together, so the steps between faces only shrink.
+
+The alternative in the brief (lit and mid both above 0.8, shade close under them) was not taken: it would bleach the desert and the beach to cream, and a ground that bright leaves the fighters' auras (20 CIEDE2000) with nothing to stand against.
+
+## The new ladders
+
+Drawn luminance is the relative luminance of the stored colour times 1.10 per channel, as measured above. Step is the difference between neighbouring faces; spread is lit minus shade.
+
+| Biome | Face | Stored | Drawn luminance | Step | Face distance (CIEDE2000) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Desert | lit | #cfc17d | 0.654 | 0.036 | 6.1 to mid |
+| | mid | #d9b868 | 0.618 | 0.034 | 8.2 to shade |
+| | shade | #ebac51 | 0.584 | spread **0.070** | |
+| Beach | lit | #cdc392 | 0.673 | 0.033 | 4.9 |
+| | mid | #d4bc84 | 0.640 | 0.035 | 7.2 |
+| | shade | #e1b172 | 0.605 | spread **0.069** | |
+| Savanna | lit | #b7af62 | 0.516 | 0.034 | 5.7 |
+| | mid | #bfa64f | 0.483 | 0.037 | 9.1 |
+| | shade | #d0982c | 0.445 | spread **0.071** | |
+| Plains | lit | #8ba427 | 0.396 | 0.030 | 7.9 |
+| | mid | #70a245 | 0.366 | 0.034 | 7.8 |
+| | shade | #39a14c | 0.331 | spread **0.064** | |
+
+Before: the spreads were desert 0.475, beach 0.441, savanna 0.420 and plains 0.326. The desert's mid is the same as before (0.617 to 0.618), so the warm sand keeps its centre; the mesas, rock, vegetation and subsoil are unchanged. The plains' lit green is more saturated than a plain hue shift gives because the tritan check (a preset aura against every tone, 14 CIEDE2000) failed the duller greens by 0.4 to 1.2.
+
+## The scar's fill on sand
+
+The beam's glass band was a dark green-black (#1f3d38, luminance 0.039) with a pale edge; panned across the sand it flipped 90k to 110k pixels a tick (ticks 609 to 634). The scar is drawn after the depth step, so its value is as stored. It is now a **pale sea-glass at about the sand's value**, so a pan across it changes by under 0.1 against the sand at the front and middle depth steps:
+
+| | Fill | Luminance | Edge | Luminance |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Desert | #a3cebe (was #1f3d38) | 0.556 (was 0.039) | #beded6 (was #bfe0d8) | 0.680 (was 0.693) |
+| Beach | #a6d0c0 (was #1f3d38) | 0.570 (was 0.039) | #c1e1d8 (was #bfe0d8) | 0.701 (was 0.693) |
+
+Against the desert's faces at the front step (0.654, 0.618, 0.584) the fill is 0.098, 0.062 and 0.028 away; at the middle step (0.55, 0.52, 0.50) it is within 0.06; the back step's far strip (0.46 to 0.42) is 0.10 to 0.14 away and small. The scar now reads by its sea-green hue and its flat edge, not by darkness: **this changes how a beam on sand looks**, so it needs the side-by-side and Orb's eye. If Orb wants it darker, any fill more than 0.1 under the sand's faces at the front step is a change the analyser counts when the band is panned across.
+
+## Not changed, and what it means
+
+- **The dark scars on the grounds that are not sand** (grass, red earth, loam, rock: luminance 0.012) still step 0.35 to 0.5 against their ground, and the other eleven grounds (forest, mountains, jungle, tundra, taiga, wetland, highland, volcanic, ocean and the two ices) still have spreads of 0.10 to 0.88 as drawn. They are not in the signature clip's path and are outside the brief, so I left them. The ices are the other large one (white against slate, 0.88). If another clip fails the same way, the same cut applies. `ground.mjs` prints the table for all fifteen.
+- **Rock** (the desert's mesas and boulders against the sand) is a different layer and still steps about 0.35 from the ground where rock begins by slope. Not in Rendering's flip map as a commonest flip; if the clip's next failing second is a rock edge, that is the next lever.
+
+## Gates run
+
+`node tools/validate.js`: 277 files, 0 errors. The biome generator's readability and colour-vision checks: desert worst aura 26.2 and worst body 15.6 (the dawn key, as before); savanna 26.7 and 21.5; beach 20.6 and 22.8; plains 23.0 and 23.4; colour vision protan, deutan and tritan at or above 14 for desert, savanna and plains (the beach's two water tones stay at 8.9 to 9.0 under protan and deutan, a known lane issue in `biomes.md` section 3). Orbit separation unchanged.
+
+## Second pass: the crater's inside and the desert rock (2026-10-27, evening; the colours below were superseded by the adjustment that follows)
+
+The ladders cleared the split's opening and the scar; the worst second moved to ticks 1140 to 1260, where the beam's impact crater flips against the sand as the right pane's camera follows the flung fighter (the crater's inside about 0.25, its rock walls about 0.44, the sand 0.58; Rendering's notes: `docs/rendering/pending/2026-10-27k/README.md`). Same rule as the ladders: tone on tone within `PATTERN_BUDGET` (0.085), told apart by hue. Tools: `ground.mjs crater`, `ground.mjs beachsub`.
+
+**The desert rock** (the lit, mid and shade of every rock face and the mesa and boulder cover) is now a terracotta at the sand's own value. Hue carries it: pale peach to coral against the sand's gold (CIEDE2000 19 to 24 from the sand face of the same tone, 6 apart from each other).
+
+| Face | Was | Now | Drawn luminance (front step) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| lit | #d29a5a | #fdb88e | 0.659 (sand lit 0.654) |
+| mid | #b87a44 | #feaf93 | 0.620 (sand mid 0.618) |
+| shade | #8a5634 | #fda79b | 0.585 (sand shade 0.584) |
+
+Rock against sand, any pair, at the five depth steps (1.10, 1.07, 1.02, 0.97, 0.94): at most 0.075, 0.080, 0.095, 0.084 and 0.080. Rock spread 0.074 at the front, less behind. The desert's far mesas keep their old colour (`derive.mjs` `FAR_BASE`): the far ridges are hazed from the old mid, so the far ladder is byte-identical.
+
+**The crater's inside** is no longer the one subsoil colour with a lite and a dark derived from it in the render (lite 0.14, dark 0.3: a spread of 0.36 on the desert). It carries its three faces as data, `palette.subsoil_faces`, for the desert and the beach only:
+
+| Biome | Face | Stored | Luminance (the inside is drawn after the depth step, as stored) | Distance from the sand face of that tone (CIEDE2000) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Desert | lit | #f6c46c | 0.602 | 10.5 |
+| | mid | #febb71 | 0.578 | 10.4 |
+| | shade | #feb582 | 0.557 | 10.6 |
+| Beach | lit | #e6d3a8 | 0.662 | 5.9 |
+| | mid | #f5ca9a | 0.640 | 8.3 |
+| | shade | #fec199 | 0.615 | 9.8 |
+
